AB  - Music may be one of the most longstanding neuromodulators across world cultures. This chapter briefly notes historical uses of music in Ancient Greece, Egypt, India, China, Peru and the African continent. Techniques that use music as neuro-stimulation and neuro-destimulation are discussed. Specific techniques considered include: Melodic Intonation Therapy, Guided imagery with Music, Bio-guided Music Therapy, Brain Music Therapy, Native Flute Biofeedback and Vocal Toning. Pilot qEEG brain maps are displayed for conditions of vocal toning, Tibetan bowls and reclining on a 50 string sound bed during playing of the strings.
