AB  - Introduction
The aim of this study is to sort out and summarize the research hotspots and development trends of basketball injury globally.
Method
The author used VOSviewer visualization software to visually analyze academic literature on basketball injury, which is retrieved from Web of Science. Our findings can provide help for the development of the field of basketball injury in China.
Results
The results showed that: (1) The number of articles on basketball sports injury showed a wave-like rise; highly cited articles mainly focused on the knee joint (main anterior cruciate ligament) injury and brain concussion.; the research field had become a multi-science interdisciplinary field with sports science as the main body and medicine (mainly bone science and rehabilitation), engineering, psychology, and other disciplines as an auxiliary. (2) The research force was concentrated in European and American countries, and the United States had the largest number of articles; the main institutions of publication were colleges and universities. (3) The hot spots were closely related to lower limb sports injury and prevention, characteristics of sports injury, rehabilitation treatment, return to sport, wheelchair basketball, involving injury prevention, epidemiology, biomechanics, kinematics, women's and youth basketball and other aspects (4) The research trends are divided into four stages according to the amount of published papers and future research trends are predicted.
Discussion
Firstly, basic research is continued to explore the mechanism of injury occurrence and prevention through advanced research methods; Secondly, clinical research constantly put forward new rehabilitation treatment methods to promote the return of players to sports.
